OL,3,GFEATURES C1968 ITV changes: beginning
OL,4,Cof a golden age
OL,5,
OL,6,FThere's no point going over old ground.
OL,7,FWider technological changes mean that a
OL,8,Fnational ITV service with a
OL,9,Fmarket-driven schedule would have
OL,10,Fhappened eventually by one path or
OL,11,Fanother, even without disruptive and
OL,12,Fmisguided political interference in the
OL,13,Fform of the 1990 Broadcasting Act.
OL,14,
OL,15,FBut it is worth celebrating the 1968
OL,16,Fchanges and their legacy.
OL,17,
OL,18,FPart of their legacy is, simply, that
OL,19,Fthings after 1993 could have been a
OL,20,Flot, lot worse.
OL,21,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBRewindCNat TVFOn This Day
FL,138,120,200,120,0,100@
